      "decision_template": "Master-slave transmission gate DFF (W_TG={w_tg}um, W_INV={w_inv}um, L={l_val}um)",
      "reason": "Transmission gate latches have ~30% lower CLK-to-Q delay compared to NAND-based DFFs of equal drive strength because the pass path uses complementary PMOS+NMOS in parallel, halving the effective on-resistance without doubling gate loading.",
      "tradeoffs": "Requires both CLK and CLKN (inverted clock). The clock inverter (M_INV3) adds a small skew between CLK and CLKN that must be balanced in the layout.",
